<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tsushima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tsushima was a naval battle fought in May 1905 in the strait between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, the decisive engagement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a>. The Japanese fleet under Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togo">Togo</a> destroyed the Russian fleet that had sailed from the Baltic. The defeat was a humiliation for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and contributed to the unrest of the 1905 revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tsushima.jpg" alt="Battle of Tsushima" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tōjō Shōtarō · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Tsushima,_1905_by_T%C5%8Dj%C5%8D_Sh%C5%8Dtar%C5%8D.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Before the <b>Battle of Tsushima</b> in 1905, Russia's Baltic Fleet sailed some 18,000 nautical miles around the world, only to be annihilated by Japan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
